    "commit": "7a68f9c3d",
    "summary": "Module-state inventory for the threaded daemon: a test-side compiler scanner lists the 290 module-scope mutable declarations a session worker loads; a reviewed fixture classifies each (per-thread, shared-store, or one-owner with its thread) with a reason; a guard test over the repo fails on any new, stale or invalid entry (it already caught one during t6). Seven values needed a single copy; per the user's decision all four problems were moved inline: models.* and codeReview.* (plus step.call for insrc_code_review_step) run on the shared-state worker; tools.config.set is served on main, which pushes tool settings to every worker; analyze.run.status/purge are routed to the thread running the run via the status board, fixing a status served elsewhere that rewrote a running analysis as abandoned. Manual code review; no daemon code review. Code review (manual): no HIGH/MED findings; LOW notes: tools.config.set on main now builds main's lazy handler runtime at the IDE's connect; a tool loop starting between a settings change and its push reads the previous settings; two threads running the same analyze run id keep only the latest owner on the board; code review and model checks now share the shared-state worker with chat, todos and understanding. Full sweep: 6961 tests, 15 failed, none from this Story: 6 timing/perf checks that pass alone, the known SIGTERM boot flake, the pre-existing file-tools test, and the other session's CM-S1/CM-S3/CM-S4 connection-management checks (session-probe fails identically with this Story's t6 reverted in an isolated worktree)."
